dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, anna. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing alright. how about you?
[doctor] i'm doing well. so, i know that the nurse told you about dax. i'd like to tell dax a little bit about you. hey, dragon, i'm seeing a patient here, anna, and she's a 26-year-old female. she's got a past medical history of epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease. and she's coming in today because she's got some joint pain.
[patient] yes, my left elbow has really been bothering me.
[doctor] okay. so, tell me a little bit about what's going on with your elbow. what's been going on?
[patient] well, i sit at a desk all day for work and my elbows are always bent. and then after work, it's really hard for me to flex and extend my left elbow. it's been really stiff and painful. and i've noticed some swelling on the back of my elbow, my olecranon. i'm right-handed, so i can still write, which is great. but typing is really difficult. i don't have any numbness or tingling in my hands, but i do have some weakness in my arm, but nothing too significant. and i don't have any fever or chills.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any recent seizures?
[patient] no, i haven't had any recent seizures. my last seizure was about a year ago.
[doctor] okay. and are you still taking your medication for that?
[patient] yes, i am. i'm still taking keppra.
[doctor] okay. and what about your depression? how are you doing with that?
[patient] i started therapy last year and i'm trying to avoid medications for this problem. i'm doing well with therapy, but i still feel down and stressed. i don't have any suicidal or homicidal ideations.
[doctor] okay. and then for your peptic ulcer, how are you doing with that?
[patient] i was dealing with a lot of stress last year and then i had an endoscopy and it showed that i had an episode of gastritis. and then i was diagnosed with peptic ulcer disease and started on protonix. and everything has been good since the procedure.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any abdominal pain or nausea or vomiting?
[patient] no, i don't have any of those symptoms. i do have a little bit of a runny nose and some nasal congestion from allergies.
[doctor] okay. well, let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam. so, on your physical exam, i do appreciate some swelling and erythema of your left elbow. and when i palpate it, it's tender to the touch. and it's warm to the touch. and when i flex and extend your elbow, it's painful. and i do appreciate a palpable left radial pulse. i also reviewed the results of your left arm x-ray and it does not show any evidence of an elbow fracture. and your ekg from a year ago was normal. and your endoscopy showed an episode of gastritis.
[patient] mm-hmm.
[doctor] so, for your first problem of your left elbow pain, i think you have left olecranon bursitis caused by repetitive trauma from sitting at your desk. i'm going to start you on meloxicam, 15 milligrams once a day. i want you to use a pillow to rest your arm on. you may also ice the area. does that sound okay?
[patient] yes, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. and i want to continue you on your keppra, 500 milligrams twice a day. i'm going to refill that for you today. and then for your depression, i'm going to start you on lexapro, 10 milligrams once a day. and then for your peptic ulcer disease, i want you to continue on the protonix, 40 milligrams once a day before meals.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] any questions?
[patient] no, that's it. thank you.
[doctor] okay. hey, dragon, I'm going to go ahead and finalize the note. }}<|eot_id|>
