dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, teresa. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i'm here for my elbow.
[doctor] okay. so i see that you're here for your right elbow. tell me a little bit about what's going on.
[patient] yeah, so it started about four days ago and it's been bothering me a lot. i can't use my pottery wheel anymore, which is kind of a bummer because i really like to make things for my kids. so i'm here to see if there's anything i can do about it.
[doctor] okay. and you said it started four days ago?
[patient] yeah, yeah, it just started out as like a little bit of pain and now it's really bothering me.
[doctor] okay. and have you tried anything to help with the pain?
[patient] yeah, i've tried ice and ibuprofen, but nothing seems to be helping.
[doctor] okay. and have you done anything to hurt your elbow recently?
[patient] i don't think so. i've just been using my pottery wheel a lot more.
[doctor] okay. so you've increased your use of the pottery wheel?
[patient] yeah, i have.
[doctor] okay. and how would you rate your pain on a scale of one to ten?
[patient] probably a seven.
[doctor] okay. and does it radiate anywhere else?
[patient] it goes down my arm a little bit.
[doctor] okay. and does it wake you up at night?
[patient] yeah, if i roll over it wakes me up.
[doctor] okay. all right. well, let's go ahead and take a look. so i'm just gon na examine your right elbow here. i'm gon na press on the inside of your elbow. does that hurt?
[patient] yeah, it hurts a little bit.
[doctor] okay. and i'm gon na press on the outside of your elbow. does that hurt?
[patient] not so much.
[doctor] okay. and i'm gon na bend your wrist up and down. does that hurt?
[patient] yeah, that hurts.
[doctor] okay. and i'm gon na bend it the other way. does that hurt?
[patient] a little bit.
[doctor] okay. and i'm gon na bend your wrist up and down again. does that hurt?
[patient] yeah, that hurts a little bit.
[doctor] okay. so it sounds like you have some tendinitis in your elbow. we'll go ahead and take some x-rays. and it looks like you have some tendinitis in your elbow. and we'll go ahead and treat that with a sling, ice, ibuprofen, and rest. and we'll see you in two weeks and check on how you're doing.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i'm gon na go ahead and increase your metformin to 1,000 milligrams twice a day. and i think it would be a good idea to see a diabetic educator for more information on managing your diabetes.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i'm going to order a hemoglobin a1c to get a more accurate assessment of your blood sugar levels.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and keep taking your lisinopril. and just keep walking every day.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right. any questions?
[patient] no, i think you covered everything.
[doctor] okay. great. i'll see you in two weeks.
[patient] okay, thank you.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
