dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi greg how are you today
[patient] i'm doing okay i'm a little sore
[doctor] good to see you today so i know that dr. tucker told you about dax but i just wanted to go over a few things with you so i reviewed my notes and it looks like you've been having some knee issues
[patient] mm-hmm
[doctor] can you tell me a little bit about what happened
[patient] yeah so about two and a half weeks ago i was walking down the street and i stepped off of a curb and turned over my ankle and i've been having some issues with my knee since then
[doctor] okay and so what part of your knee are you having pain in
[patient] it's on the outside of my knee
[doctor] okay and do you have pain with every step or is it just when you stand on one foot for a long time
[patient] no i'm okay with walking unless i stand on one foot for a long time
[doctor] okay and you said you've been having some issues with your knee for two and a half weeks
[patient] yeah
[doctor] okay and how have you been treating it
[patient] i've been taking ibuprofen and i've been icing it about four times a day
[doctor] okay and has that been helping you
[patient] it's been helping me in the morning and at the end of the day but not so much at night
[doctor] okay and have you noticed any numbness or tingling in your foot
[patient] yeah i have
[doctor] okay and is that a new symptom or
[patient] no it's not new
[doctor] okay and have you had any problems with your toes in the past
[patient] yeah i've had a couple of problems with my toes over the years i've actually broken my second toe i think three times in the last ten years
[doctor] okay so i'm just gon na do a quick physical exam of your knee and i do appreciate some edema and effusion on the outside of your knee does that hurt
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and when i push on the outside of your knee does that hurt
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and i'm gon na do a little test called the varus test and that's positive so that means your knee tucks in a little bit when i push on the outside of your knee so that's consistent with a lateral collateral ligament strain so let me show you my results and then we'll talk about our plan
[patient] okay
[doctor] so your x-rays did not show any evidence of any fractures or dislocations or any bony abnormalities so that's a good thing so i'm gon na put you in formal physical therapy to help strengthen your knee and i'm gon na prescribe you some meloxicam fifteen milligrams a day to help with the pain so if your pain does not improve with physical therapy i'm gon na recommend getting an mri so what do you think
[patient] that sounds good
[doctor] alright so i'm gon na go ahead and order those things and we'll get you set up with physical therapy and we'll see you back in about four to six weeks
[patient] okay
[doctor] alright take care
[patient] thank you
[doctor] you're welcome }}<|eot_id|>
