dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, i'm doctor shah. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing well, thank you.
[doctor] good to hear that. so, i see here that you're in for a visit today for your hypercholesterolemia. how's that going?
[patient] it's going well. i've been doing some research and i'm trying to make some dietary changes.
[doctor] okay, that's great. so, i know you're an active person. you like riding your bike. how's that going?
[patient] yeah, i like riding my bike. i like going on trails.
[doctor] okay. that's good. i'm glad to hear that. and how about your parents? did they smoke?
[patient] yeah, they did.
[doctor] okay. so, i know you've had some cholesterol levels done in the past. can you tell me a little bit about those?
[patient] yeah, i had a cholesterol level done recently and it was a little high.
[doctor] okay, so it looks like it's about 210. so, we're going to need to take a look at that and see what we can do about it. so, i know you had a cousin that passed away from a heart attack. is that correct?
[patient] yeah, that's correct.
[doctor] okay. and do you know how old they were when they had the heart attack?
[patient] they were in their 40's.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any family history of hypercholesterolemia?
[patient] no, not that i know of.
[doctor] okay. and have you ever smoked?
[patient] no, i've never smoked.
[doctor] okay. that's good. and you live with your parents? is that right?
[patient] i did, but i moved out.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm just gon na do a quick physical exam. so, on your physical exam, i'm gon na listen to your heart and lungs and your abdomen. everything looks good. there's no hepatomegaly or splenomegaly. your neck is supple without thyromegaly. on your eyes, no xanthomas noted. your blood pressure looks good. your heart exam is normal. no murmurs, gallops, or rubs. your lungs are clear bilaterally. so, i do want to order some blood work. i'm gon na order a full cholesterol panel, hemoglobin a1c, a cmp, a thyroid study, and a liver panel. we'll also order some genetic testing to see if there's a genetic component to your elevated cholesterol. i'd like to refer you to a nutritionist to help you with your diet. and then we'll follow up in about three to six months after you've seen the nutritionist and we'll check your cholesterol again.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] any questions?
[patient] no, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. }}<|eot_id|>
