dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, miss taylor. how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay.
[doctor] good. so i know the nurse told you what's going on. i just wanted to see you in and talk to you about your chest pain.
[patient] mm-hmm.
[doctor] so i know that you've been having some chest pain. can you tell me a little bit more about that?
[patient] yeah. i've been having it for a few weeks now. it's usually when i'm doing something physical. it's like a tightness and then it becomes a sharp pain.
[doctor] okay. and when you have that pain, do you feel short of breath or anything like that?
[patient] no, not really.
[doctor] okay. and have you ever taken any of those nitroglycerin tablets that we have in the office?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. have you ever had any dizziness or nausea or vomiting?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. all right. and what about sweating or clamminess?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. all right. and have you had this type of pain before?
[patient] no, this is the first time.
[doctor] okay. and do you have a family history of heart disease?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay. all right. well, i know that you have diabetes, so i'm a little worried that you might have a blockage in one of your arteries. we'll do some more tests to check.
[patient] mm-hmm.
[doctor] so i'm going to put you on some baby aspirin, 81 milligrams a day. i'm also going to give you a prescription for some nitroglycerin. take up to three tablets every five minutes if you're having that pain.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and i'm also going to start you on a blood pressure medication called hydrochlorothiazide, just to help with some of the swelling that i saw on your exam today.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] i'm also going to order a hemoglobin a1c. i want to make sure your diabetes is under control. i want you to follow up with me in two weeks. we'll recheck your blood pressure and your hemoglobin a1c and go from there.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i think you covered everything.
[doctor] okay. all right. well, i'll see you in two weeks then.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] hey, dragon, show me the hemoglobin a1c. i'm sorry, dragon, show me the results. hey, dragon, show me the results. okay, so your hemoglobin a1c is 7.0. that's good. so that's, that's great. i'm going to send in a prescription for your diabetes medication. i want you to continue taking the metformin 500 milligrams twice a day. i want you to follow up with ophthalmology for that diabetic retinopathy exam. i'm going to order a repeat hemoglobin a1c in two weeks. i want you to keep taking the metformin and make some dietary modifications. any questions?
[patient] no, i think that's all good.
[doctor] okay. hey, dragon, order and print the hemoglobin a1c and the prescriptions. hey, dragon, order and print the prescriptions. }}<|eot_id|>
