dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi sophia how are you today
[patient] i'm doing okay i'm just really happy to be here
[doctor] great i'm glad to see you i see you were referred to me by your primary care physician for some knee pain
[patient] mm-hmm
[doctor] so can you tell me a little bit about your knee pain
[patient] yeah so it's been going on for about six months now and i'm not really sure what caused it
[doctor] okay and have you had any injuries to your knees in the past
[patient] no i don't think so
[doctor] okay and describe the pain to me what does it feel like
[patient] it's kind of like a deep achy pain
[doctor] okay and where is the pain located
[patient] it's kind of in the back of my knees
[doctor] okay and have you noticed any swelling or redness in your knees
[patient] no not really
[doctor] okay and does anything make the pain better or worse
[patient] yeah so when i'm sitting and then i stand up it hurts a lot and then going up and down the stairs is really hard
[doctor] okay and how do you usually feel after you've been standing for a while
[patient] it's just kind of sore and then i feel like i need to sit down
[doctor] okay and have you tried anything for the pain
[patient] yeah i've been putting ice on it and wrapping it with an ace bandage and i've been taking ibuprofen and aleve
[doctor] okay and what type of activities do you like to do
[patient] i like to run
[doctor] okay and how far can you run
[patient] i used to be able to run like five to six miles a day but now i can barely make it like. five
[doctor] okay and have you had any injuries to your knees in the past
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and do you remember if you've had any other medical problems in the past
[patient] i had a fracture in my arm when i was in sixth grade
[doctor] okay and have you noticed any creaking or popping in your knees
[patient] yeah i do
[doctor] okay
[patient] it's almost like a clicking sound
[doctor] okay and have you noticed any weakness in your legs
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and have you noticed any difficulty with your balance
[patient] no
[doctor] okay great well i'm gon na go ahead and examine you now and i'm just gon na check your vital signs first
[patient] okay
[doctor] so your blood pressure is one twenty over seventy five and your heart rate is seventy four which is all within normal limits i'm gon na go ahead and examine you now so i'm just gon na check your gait and i'm not going to see any deformities so that's good your cardiovascular exam is regular rate and rhythm no murmurs and there's no edema on your lower extremities i'm gon na go ahead and check your strength now your patella and achilles reflexes are symmetrical so that's good and on your lower extremity exam your abduction strength is three out of five but the rest of your muscle strength is five out of five on your knee exam there's no overlying erythema ecchymosis or warmth of the skin and there's no effusion but you do have tenderness to palpation of the bilateral retinaculum and you do have a positive patellar grind test you do have knee pain with squatting but your lachman test is negative bilaterally and your anterior and posterior drawer tests are negative bilaterally and your mcmurray test is negative bilaterally and i've reviewed your x-rays of your bilateral knees and these demonstrate no evidence of any fractures or osteoarthritis so based on your exam and your radiographic findings i think you have patellofemoral pain syndrome so i'm gon na explain that to you real quick so patellofemoral pain syndrome is a condition where you have pain in the front of your knees and it's usually from the way you walk or run or stand so i think that's what's going on with you so i would like to start you on some physical therapy to increase your lower extremity strength and mobility and to correct any incorrect running mechanics and i would like you to take it easy on the running and you can continue taking the ibuprofen or aleve as needed for pain and all your questions
[patient] okay so i'm going to start physical therapy and stop running for a while
[doctor] that's right and we'll see you soon
[patient] okay great
[doctor] thank you
[patient] thank you
[doctor] you're welcome }}<|eot_id|>
