dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi kyle how are you
[patient] i'm doing okay
[doctor] so i see here that you're here for an evaluation of low back pain
[patient] yeah
[doctor] okay so tell me about when did this start
[patient] it started about two weeks ago
[doctor] okay and what were you doing
[patient] i was lifting a box of books
[doctor] okay and what happened
[patient] i felt a pop and it's been aching and sharp since then
[doctor] okay and has it been getting worse
[patient] yeah it has
[doctor] okay and does it radiate anywhere
[patient] it radiates down my left leg
[doctor] okay and does it hurt when you sit
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and what do you do for work
[patient] i have a sedentary job
[doctor] okay and does the pain affect your job
[patient] no it doesn't but i don't feel like i should be as active as i used to be
[doctor] okay and do you exercise at all
[patient] a little bit a few times a week but i'm not consistent
[doctor] okay and any numbness or tingling or weakness or loss of control of your bladder or bowel movements
[patient] no
[doctor] okay all right and have you tried any medications for the pain
[patient] i've been taking ibuprofen and tylenol
[doctor] okay and does that help
[patient] it helps a little bit
[doctor] okay and have you ever been evaluated for surgery
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and do you smoke
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and have you ever played any sports
[patient] i played soccer in the midfield position
[doctor] okay and i see that your father has back pain
[patient] yes
[doctor] okay all right so i'm gon na go ahead and examine you now your vitals look good your blood pressure is one thirty over seventy your heart and lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally i don't appreciate any murmurs rubs or gallops on your heart exam i don't see any evidence of trauma or deformity on your back exam i do see some midline tenderness at the l four to five disc space with right-sided lumbar paravertebral tenderness and pain with lumbar flexion and i do get a positive straight leg test in your left leg so i'm gon na go ahead and look at your results so your mri of the lumbar spine showed some disc desiccation and a disc bulge with a paracentral disc herniation resulting in moderate right neural foraminal stenosis so what does all of that mean kyle so it means that you have a herniated disc in your back which is causing the pain and the pain is radiating down your left leg and it's causing some nerve irritation so i think the best course of treatment is going to be a corticosteroid injection which will help with the inflammation and the pain and it's a very safe procedure the risks are bleeding infection nerve damage blood vessel damage reaction to the medication including skin changes swelling and elevated glucose levels if you're diabetic so do you have any questions for me
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and i'll go ahead and call in the nurse and we'll get you ready for the injection
[patient] okay
[doctor] all right thank you
[patient] thank you }}<|eot_id|>
