dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi angela how are you doing today
[patient] i'm doing okay thanks how are you
[doctor] i'm doing good i'm good to see you today what brings you into the clinic today
[patient] my knee hurts
[doctor] okay what knee hurts
[patient] my left knee
[doctor] okay left knee okay tell me what happened to your left knee
[patient] i was running around with my niece and i fell and i heard a pop and i twisted my knee
[doctor] okay and when did this happen
[patient] it was about a week ago
[doctor] okay a week ago okay and have you been limping since then
[patient] yes i have
[doctor] okay and where is the pain located on your knee
[patient] it's on the inside and the outside
[doctor] okay okay and how would you rate your pain on a scale of one to ten with ten being the worst pain you've ever felt
[patient] it's about a four
[doctor] okay and is it a throbbing pain
[patient] yes it is
[doctor] okay and have you taken anything for the pain
[patient] i've taken tylenol and it helps a little bit i've also wrapped my knee with some kinesiology tape
[doctor] okay and have you tried ibuprofen
[patient] i can't take ibuprofen i have an ulcer
[doctor] okay okay i see alright so let's take a look at your knee i'm gon na do a physical exam of your left knee okay so i'm gon na press right here and i'm gon na press here and does it hurt
[patient] yes
[doctor] okay and i'm gon na bend your knee and does that hurt
[patient] yes
[doctor] okay and i'm gon na extend it and does that hurt
[patient] yes
[doctor] okay and i'm gon na push in here and does that hurt
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and i'm gon na push here and does that hurt
[patient] no
[doctor] okay so i'm gon na do a special test called the lachman's test and i'm gon na push here and does that hurt
[patient] no
[doctor] okay and i'm gon na push here and does that hurt
[patient] no
[doctor] okay so everything looks good there's some swelling and some fluid in your knee i'm gon na order some x-rays of your knee just to make sure there's no fracture or dislocation but everything looks good on the x-rays so i think you have a possible mcl strain what does that mean
[patient] i'm not sure
[doctor] so the mcl is one of the ligaments in your knee and it looks like you've strained it when you fell so i'm gon na put you in a knee immobilizer to give you some support and i'm gon na prescribe you some tramadol fifty milligrams to help with the pain and you can take tylenol as needed for breakthrough pain i want you to ice your knee three to four times a day for twenty to thirty minutes at a time and i want you to refrain from running for the next three weeks if your pain doesn't improve with the immobilizer i'm gon na recommend getting an mri
[patient] okay
[doctor] okay any questions for me
[patient] no i think that's it
[doctor] okay alright well i'll see you in about three weeks if not before
[patient] okay
[doctor] alright take care
[patient] thank you }}<|eot_id|>
